---
// src/pages/privacy-policy.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy — SweepGrid (Windows & Android)" 
  description="Read the SweepGrid privacy policy. Discover how our 100% local, offline architecture protects your personal screenshot data on Windows and Android."
>
  <div class="mesh-gradient-bg"></div>
  <div class="min-h-screen flex flex-col font-sans">
    <Header />
    
    <main class="flex-1 max-w-5xl w-full mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16 space-y-12">
      <header class="space-y-3 border-b border-hairline pb-8 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-500 font-semibold">LEGAL & PRIVACY ASSURANCE</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-display-lg text-ink font-feature-geom">
          Privacy Policy.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-body leading-relaxed">
          Your files never leave your device. Learn how Sweepgrid protects your privacy across Windows and Android.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed font-sans">
        
        <!-- 1. Local-First Architecture -->
        <div class="p-8 border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-2xl space-y-4 shadow-level-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink font-feature-geom">1. 100% Offline & Local-First Processing</h2>
          <p>
            At <strong>Sweepgrid</strong> (engineered by The Black Rose), we believe your personal files, work documents, receipts, and screen captures belong exclusively to you. Sweepgrid operates entirely as an offline, client-side utility on both Windows and Android operating systems.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you scan folders, generate thumbnails, or purge captures, all computations occur exclusively on your local device CPU and internal storage. No screenshot data, image previews, folder paths, or system metadata are ever transmitted to external cloud servers or remote databases.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. Zero Telemetry & Tracking -->
        <div class="p-8 border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-2xl space-y-4 shadow-level-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink font-feature-geom">2. Zero Telemetry & Ad Tracking</h2>
          <p>
            Sweepgrid contains zero third-party advertising SDKs, diagnostic sniffers, or user tracking cookies. We do not build demographic profiles, monitor file names, or track your workflow habits. Both the Windows desktop app and the Android APK function completely disconnected from the internet without any loss of features.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. Safe Deletion & Recycle Bin / MediaStore Trash -->
        <div class="p-8 border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-2xl space-y-4 shadow-level-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink font-feature-geom">3. File Handling & Safe Trash Safeguards</h2>
          <p>
            Sweepgrid respects your platform's native safety mechanisms:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 pt-1 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong>Windows:</strong> Deletions call native Windows Shell deletion APIs that direct files directly into your <strong>Windows Recycle Bin</strong>, allowing you to restore any accidentally deleted image.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Android:</strong> Deletions use Android Scoped Storage and the standard <strong>MediaStore API</strong> to move items into the Android system 30-day Trash bin. Items remain restorable via your Gallery or Google Photos app for 30 days.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 4. Contact & Inquiries -->
        <div class="p-8 border border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-2xl space-y-4 shadow-level-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink font-feature-geom">4. Questions & Developer Inquiries</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy or software architecture, you may contact the development team at any time via our <a href="/#contact" class="text-emerald-500 font-semibold hover:underline">Contact Page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>
